# ACTIVITY 2: DUCK TYPING

# 1a. What is duck typing?
# Duck typing allows an object to be used as long as it has
# the required method, regardless of its class or inheritance.

# 1b. What did the Car class need?
# The Car class needed to have the same method called in the
# loop so it could work with Dog and Cat without inheriting
# from the Animal class.

# 3. How does the code demonstrate polymorphism?
# The code demonstrates polymorphism because the same move()
# method behaves differently depending on the object.
# The Car drives, the Boat sails, and the Drone flies.
# All three work with start_trip() because they have
# the same move() method, even without inheritance.
